{%- comment -%}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AAO REVIEWS - page bootstrap
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Rendered once from layout/theme.liquid. Emits the widget stylesheet, the engine and the runtime
config. The engine bails out immediately (and fetches nothing) on pages that hold neither a
`.aao-reviews` widget nor a `.aao-rating` badge, so this is cheap sitewide.

Data is split across assets so no page downloads the whole corpus, and so a review set shared by
many products is stored once:

  aao-reviews-summary.json     one row per handle (~36KB). Fetched once per page that renders a
                               rating badge or the widget. Its `src` names the asset below that
                               holds each handle's review list.
  aao-reviews-store.json       the store-wide showcase set Loox served on products with no reviews
                               of their own.
  aao-reviews-set-<hash>.json  the other shared review sets.
  aao-reviews-p-<handle>.json  products that have a review set of their own.
  aao-rev-<name>.jpg           review photos, re-hosted off the Loox CDN.

All of these are produced from the harvest by docs/reviews/split_reviews.py.

There is no backend and no third-party service. New reviews are submitted through Shopify's own
contact form (server-rendered in snippets/aao-reviews-widget.liquid) and arrive as email at the
store's contact address; approved ones are added to the assets above and deployed. The baked
assets are the single source of truth for what renders.

Set `inline_summary: true` when rendering to embed the summary in the page instead of fetching it.
That removes a request on every page at the cost of ~16KB of HTML sitewide, so it is off by
default. See docs/reviews/README.md.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  PARITY vs HONESTY - the one switch worth knowing about.

  Loox padded this catalogue: of 262 products showing reviews, only 11 have a review actually
  written about them. The other 251 display a shared "showcase" feed Loox injected. Everything
  here defaults to reproducing that exactly, so cancelling the app changes nothing a customer can
  see.

  Set genuine_only below to true and every product shows only its own reviews instead. On today's
  data that means 11 products with reviews and 251 showing "Be the first to review this product".
  It is a business decision, not a technical one. See docs/reviews/README.md.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  WHERE THE DATA COMES FROM is decided in snippets/aao-reviews-flags.liquid - one boolean,
  `use_metaobjects`, false today. It lives in its own snippet because `render` scopes are isolated
  and the widget and the badge have to read the same value; they capture that snippet's output the
  same way this one does. Everything below branches on it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture aao_mode -%}{%- render 'aao-reviews-flags' -%}{%- endcapture -%}

{{ 'aao-reviews.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- if aao_mode contains 'metaobjects' -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    METAOBJECT MODE
    ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Reviews are server-rendered from metaobjects (see snippets/aao-reviews-list.liquid and
    snippets/aao-rating-badge.liquid), so nothing is fetched and the legacy engine is not loaded.
    assets/aao-reviews-mo.js only supplies behaviour: load more, histogram filter, photo lightbox,
    and the write-a-review panel toggle.

    THE ONE EXPENSIVE THING, AND WHY IT USUALLY COSTS NOTHING
    --------------------------------------------------------
    A rating badge on a product card needs its group's average and count. Averaging a 124-review
    group per card would be thousands of metaobject loads per collection page, so `aao_review_group`
    carries derived `rating_avg` / `rating_count` fields and the badge just reads them.

    A group whose `rating_count` is blank (created by hand in the admin, cache never filled) is the
    only case that needs computing, and it is computed HERE - once per page for the whole page,
    never once per card - then published as window.AAO_REVIEW_STATS for the badges to paint.

    The walk below reads the ~9 group metaobjects (two scalar fields each, no list resolution) and
    only resolves a group's review list when that group's cache is missing. With the migration's
    caches in place, no list is ever resolved and no <script> is emitted.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign aao_stats = ''
    assign aao_groups = shop.metaobjects.aao_review_group.values
  -%}

  {%- for aao_g in aao_groups -%}
    {%- if aao_g.rating_count.value != blank -%}
      {%- continue -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign aao_n = 0
      assign aao_sum = 0
      for aao_rv in aao_g.reviews.value
        if aao_rv.hidden.value == true
          continue
        endif
        assign aao_n = aao_n | plus: 1
        assign aao_sum = aao_sum | plus: aao_rv.rating.value
      endfor

      assign aao_a = 0
      if aao_n > 0
        assign aao_a = aao_sum | times: 10.0 | divided_by: aao_n | round | divided_by: 10.0
      endif

      capture aao_row
        echo aao_g.system.handle | json
        echo ':{"avg":'
        echo aao_a
        echo ',"count":'
        echo aao_n
        echo '}'
      endcapture

      if aao_stats != blank
        assign aao_stats = aao_stats | append: ','
      endif
      assign aao_stats = aao_stats | append: aao_row
    -%}
  {%- endfor -%}

  {%- if aao_stats != blank -%}
    <script>
      window.AAO_REVIEW_STATS = { {{ aao_stats }} };
    </script>
  {%- endif -%}

  <script src="{{ 'aao-reviews-mo.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{%- else -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign genuine_only = false

    comment
      The theme's asset directory, e.g. https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/.../assets/ - the engine
      builds the review-list and photo URLs from it rather than hard-coding a CDN host.
    endcomment
    assign asset_base = 'aao-reviews.css' | asset_url | split: 'aao-reviews.css' | first
  -%}

  <script>
    window.AAO_REVIEWS_CONFIG = {
      assetBase: {{ asset_base | json }},
      summaryUrl: {{ 'aao-reviews-summary.json' | asset_url | json }},
      genuineOnly: {{ genuine_only | json }}
    };
  </script>

  {%- if inline_summary -%}
    <script type="application/json" id="aao-reviews-summary-data">{{ 'aao-reviews-summary.json' | inline_asset_content }}</script>
  {%- endif -%}

  <script src="{{ 'aao-reviews.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{%- endif -%}
